+\ Process-control primitives (shell support, see PROGRESS.md). Order
+\ here must match relf.c's dispatch table exactly, since PRIMITIVE
+\ assigns tokens sequentially as each of these lines is processed.
+PRIMITIVE SYSCALL ( block num --- r )  \ one system call, its arguments in the block; the shell's OS words are Forth on it
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (EXECVE)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (WAITPID)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (PIPE)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (DUP2)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (GETENV)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (SETENV)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (SYS-EXIT)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (CHDIR)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (GETCWD)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (SYS-ARGC)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (SYS-ARG)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (GETPID)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (UNSETENV)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+\ Forth-2012 memory-allocation wordset, backed by the host's own
+\ malloc/free/realloc. This is memory OUTSIDE the image - it does not
+\ consume dictionary space and is not saved by SAVE-SYSTEM. Appended
+\ at the END of this list deliberately: primitive tokens are
+\ 1 + (position-1)*stride, so adding here leaves every existing token
+\ untouched, while inserting anywhere earlier would silently
+\ renumber them (see GOALS.md and PROGRESS.md 2026-09-01).
+PRIMITIVE ALLOCATE  ( u --- a-addr ior )
+PRIMITIVE FREE      ( a-addr --- ior )
+PRIMITIVE RESIZE    ( a-addr u --- a-addr2 ior )
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (GETPWHOME)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (GETFSIZE)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+PRIMITIVE-SLOT (SETFSIZE)          \ the shell's, in Forth (forth/shell-sysc.4)
+
+\ Iteration 242: every PRIMITIVE above, together at the start of the
+\ dictionary (the file words, SYSCALL and the memory words moved up from
+\ after BIN; their order - and so every token - unchanged), and the first
+\ word after them a marker: a word is a primitive exactly when its xt is below
+\ (PRIMITIVES-END)'s. COMPILE, asks this instead of reading the primitive
+\ bit through >NAME, whose scan back from the code crossed the name - a
+\ UTF-8 name's bytes (bit 7 set) stopped it, and one with bit 5 set read as
+\ a primitive's count byte. (PRIMITIVES-END) marks the place: a variable,
+\ so the address it gives is the running image's own in every encoding (a
+\ ticked literal here would be the cross-compiler's, START-relative, and the
+\ converter would not know it for an address). Its own xt reads as a
+\ primitive's - it is never compiled.
+VARIABLE (PRIMITIVES-END)
+: PRIMITIVE? ( xt --- flag )  (PRIMITIVES-END) U< ;
+
